              "negate": false,
              "optional": true,
              "required": false,
              "variadic": false,
            },
            {
              "attributeName": "breaker",
              "defaultValue": true,
              "description": "The failure breaker, which pauses the Batch when a flaw its jobs share shows, after a few jobs instead of after all of them. The Batch's first \`canary\` jobs (5 by default), its Canary, run before the rest are released, and any of them failing pauses the Batch. After that, it pauses when more than \`maxFailurePercent\` (10 by default) of the jobs ended since the Canary began have failed. A job counts once, by its latest end; a job that a limit stopped counts as failed, while a cancelled job, or one its Runner's removal ended, does not count. Resuming a pause the breaker made starts a new Canary of the next \`canary\` jobs, those added later included. \`canary: 0\` releases every job at once, and the percentage then judges from the first job to end, so one early failure still pauses the Batch; \`maxFailurePercent: 100\` keeps the Canary alone. \`true\` by default, for the defaults; \`false\` turns the breaker off.; Any of: [{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"object","properties":{"canary":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2147483647},"maxFailurePercent":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":100}}}]",
