        {
          "arguments": [],
          "commands": [],
          "description": "Adds jobs to a Batch, at most 100 per request, each running the Batch's agent on its own \`input\` and files, and answers with the Batch and each job in the order given, with whether this add created it. An add is all or nothing: any problem refuses the whole request, naming every problem with its path, such as \`jobs[17].input\`: 400 when any job is invalid, then 409 when the Batch is cancelled and the add would create a job, then 422 for each \`customId\` the Batch already has for a job with other content. A job whose \`customId\` the Batch already has with the same content is returned as it is, with \`created: false\`, so an add can be retried safely, and a whole Batch added again to add only the jobs it lacks; a new job needs a new \`customId\`. Jobs added to a paused Batch wait for it.",
